// kalman2d_predict.eml -- N-D Kalman covariance propagation (predict step).
//
//   P' = F * P * transpose(F) + Q
//
// The MATRIX generalization of kalman_1d's scalar variance drift
// (`p + q`): a full covariance matrix pushed forward through the state-
// transition F and inflated by the process-noise covariance Q. This is
// the predict half of every multi-state Kalman filter -- a constant-
// velocity tracker (position + velocity), an IMU attitude estimator, a
// battery state-of-charge + internal-resistance model.
//
// eml-stdlib's first MATRIX-OPERATOR kernel. The body is written the way
// the math is written -- `F * P * transpose(F) + Q` -- and the compiler
// lowers the operators (matmul, transpose, matrix-add) to the flat
// per-element form every backend already emits. One source becomes C /
// Rust / C++ / Java / ... AND a machine-checked Lean theorem, and is
// regression-gated to ULP across every target with a real toolchain
// (tests/equivalence/test_matrix_cross_target.py).
//
// The @verify contract is the DEEPEST structural invariant of a covariance
// matrix: POSITIVE-SEMIDEFINITENESS is preserved. A covariance must be PSD
// (every variance, in every direction, is non-negative); a filter whose
// predict step produces a non-PSD P' is broken -- the Kalman gain can go
// negative and the estimate diverges. Given PSD prior P and PSD process
// noise Q, the congruence-plus-noise F*P*Fᵀ + Q stays PSD.
//
// Proven sorryAx-free AND classical-axiom-free (mach_ring) via the
// quadratic-form definition of PSD -- zᵀ·result·z >= 0 for all z -- which
// makes the proof a clean SUBSTITUTION, not completing-the-square:
//
//     zᵀ(F·P·Fᵀ + Q)z = (Fᵀz)ᵀ P (Fᵀz) + zᵀ Q z
//
// a sum of two non-negatives (instantiate P's PSD hypothesis at w = Fᵀz,
// Q's at z). This is the congruence theorem, machine-checked.
//
// (SYMMETRY is separately provable via the cross-element-equation path, and
// entrywise non-negativity via mach_sign. The numeric cross-target-
// equivalence gate pins the arithmetic itself to ULP across every target.)

module kalman2d_predict;

@verify(lean, theorem = "kalman2d_cov_predict_psd")
fn cov_predict(F: Mat<2,2>, P: Mat<2,2>, Q: Mat<2,2>) -> Mat<2,2>
    where chain_order <= 0
    requires (psd(P))
    requires (psd(Q))
    ensures (psd(result))
{
    F * P * transpose(F) + Q
}
